<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_BloomBurst — EXPLOSIVE_PLANT_GROWTH_1's half of the FLOOD_WITNESS_EVENT_1
    contract (explosive_plant_growth_design.md §5 "The contract"): the map-scale
    invocation. It soaks every floor cell the flood wetted, sows bloom-crop
    sprouts on the fresh soil, and the engine runs soak → charge → top in carpet
    synchrony over the following day. The quest passes nothing but the map.

    baseChance 0: never fires on its own — only a quest (or dev mode) calls it.
    The quest itself is FLOOD_WITNESS_EVENT_1's to build; this def is real now,
    so that quest's stub-degrades-gracefully branch is simply never taken.
    Worker: RimMandrake.ExplosiveGrowth.RM_IncidentWorker_BloomBurst (RM tier);
    the campaign names the bloom plant (RUT_BloomCrop, a BURST plant).
  -->
  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RUT_BloomBurst</defName>
    <label>bloom</label>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
      <li>Map_TempIncident</li>
      <li>Map_Misc</li>
    </targetTags>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.ExplosiveGrowth.RM_IncidentWorker_BloomBurst</workerClass>
    <baseChance>0</baseChance>
    <letterLabel>The bloom</letterLabel>
    <letterText>The flood's ground is erupting in bloom crop. Every sprout on the wet floor rose at once, and they will ripen, swell and burst together over the coming hours — a valley going off like popcorn.\n\nHarvest early for a swollen crop, or stand well back from anything trembling.</letterText>
    <letterDef>NeutralEvent</letterDef>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.ExplosiveGrowth.RM_BloomBurstExtension">
        <bloomPlant>RUT_BloomCrop</bloomPlant>
        <sowChance>0.6</sowChance>
        <soakHours>24</soakHours>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
